Polygonal hidden-line removal: a triangle hides nothing of a segment
outside the triangle's own box in the view (mitcad#2539, GitHub
mitcad/Mitcad#729 and #765).

A drawing's front view of a subassembly (two shafts through two upright
tubes, rollers on the shafts held by two-piece clamping collars), on the
quick path, lost the outline lines of the shafts' ends outside the left
upright at 1:2 and 1:5 (with hidden edges they were drawn hidden), and
drew them at 1:1 and 1:10. A collar half's bore has the shaft's radius;
its triangulation has a generator on the shaft's top line, and the sliver
there (9.5 long, 0.03 high in the view, seen almost edge on) lies along
the shaft's outline segment (from the shaft's end to its other end) and
almost in its plane: the segment crosses the triangle's plane inside the
collar, its points before the crossing behind the plane.

HLRAlgo_PolyData::hideByOneTriangle finds where the segment crosses the
lines of the triangle's three sides. Running along the sliver, it meets
them at a shallow angle: one crossing fell on its side and was kept, the
other fell by rounding just outside its side and was rejected (npi 0,
npiRej 1). With one crossing, the end of the segment on the inner side
was taken for inside the triangle, and the part hidden ran from the
segment's start to the plane's crossing: the whole line from the shaft's
end to the collar, 109.6 mm of the reported view. Which views meet this
depends on the triangulation, so on the view's scale.

- hideByOneTriangle cuts the part it hides to the parameters of the
  segment whose points lie in the box of the triangle's corners in the
  view (widened by the algorithm's tolerance), and hides nothing when
  none do. A triangle covers no point outside its box, so the parts
  hidden by every other triangle stay as they were.

The patch's test and its before/after proof:
third_party/vcpkg-ports/docs/opencascade-patch-tests.md, section 2539.

Upstream: new; a guard on the hidden part, the crossing logic is as it was.

diff --git a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKHLR/HLRAlgo/HLRAlgo_PolyData.cxx b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKHLR/HLRAlgo/HLRAlgo_PolyData.cxx
index b208f1b0..bd44914e 100644
--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKHLR/HLRAlgo/HLRAlgo_PolyData.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKHLR/HLRAlgo/HLRAlgo_PolyData.cxx
@@ -21,6 +21,9 @@
 
 #include <Standard_Type.hxx>
 
+#include <algorithm>
+#include <cmath>
+
 IMPLEMENT_STANDARD_RTTIEXT(HLRAlgo_PolyData, Standard_Transient)
 
 #ifdef OCCT_DEBUG
@@ -1096,6 +1099,50 @@ void HLRAlgo_PolyData::hideByOneTriangle(const HLRAlgo_BiPoint::PointsT& thePoin
     }
   }
 
+  // A triangle hides nothing of the segment outside its own box in the view.
+  // Where the segment runs along a sliver seen almost edge on and almost in
+  // its plane (the outline of a shaft along the bore of a part fitted on it),
+  // it meets the lines of the sides at a shallow angle: one crossing can fall
+  // just outside its side and be rejected while the other is kept, and with
+  // one crossing an end of the segment was taken for inside the triangle, the
+  // segment hidden from that end, far beyond the triangle (mitcad#2539).
+  {
+    const gp_XY  aP1 = thePoints.PntP12D();
+    const gp_XY  aD  = thePoints.PntP22D() - aP1;
+    const double aTol = theTriangle.Tolerance;
+    for (int aCoord = 1; aCoord <= 2; ++aCoord)
+    {
+      const double aMin =
+        std::min({theTriangle.V1.Coord(aCoord), theTriangle.V2.Coord(aCoord), theTriangle.V3.Coord(aCoord)})
+        - aTol;
+      const double aMax =
+        std::max({theTriangle.V1.Coord(aCoord), theTriangle.V2.Coord(aCoord), theTriangle.V3.Coord(aCoord)})
+        + aTol;
+      const double aFrom  = aP1.Coord(aCoord);
+      const double aAlong = aD.Coord(aCoord);
+      if (std::abs(aAlong) <= aTol)
+      {
+        if (aFrom < aMin || aFrom > aMax)
+        {
+          return;
+        }
+        continue;
+      }
+      double aT1 = (aMin - aFrom) / aAlong;
+      double aT2 = (aMax - aFrom) / aAlong;
+      if (aT1 > aT2)
+      {
+        std::swap(aT1, aT2);
+      }
+      psta = std::max(psta, aT1);
+      pend = std::min(pend, aT2);
+    }
+    if (pend - psta < theTriangle.TolParam)
+    {
+      return;
+    }
+  }
+
   bool total;
   if (psta > 0)
   {
